<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rüstringen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rüstringen was a medieval Frisian land around the Jade bay in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, before storm floods enlarged the bay. Its free peasant communities kept their own law code, the Rüstringen law, among the oldest texts in Old Frisian. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> chieftains divided it; its western part was absorbed into the Lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jever">Jever</a>, while the eastern districts fell to Oldenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rustringen.jpg" alt="Rüstringen" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Temmo Bosse · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seelanderuestringen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
